set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

/-! Variable names over `W` (TCore).  Entries are `W` terms (the literal is `(true, w)`), written with `open V W in`:
    `base v` wraps a menu variable `v : V` (`fv`, `kv`, `tp`, `ng`, `yv`, `fail` ..), `rh t f q b`, `ka t f s b`, `z0 t f`,
    `ty t f sd p1 p2 q1 q2`, `tfail t f sd [c]` are the tie variables, and gates are written with local infix notations
    (the sign of each operand): for `V` operands (inside `base`): `a AND b` is `V.gate true a true b`, `a NOR b` is
    `V.gate false a false b`, `a NOTAND b` is `V.gate false a true b`; for a gate with a non-`base` operand:
    `a WAND b` is `W.wgate true a true b`, `a WNOR b` is `W.wgate false a false b`, `a WNOTAND b` is `W.wgate false a true b`,
    `a WANDNOT b` is `W.wgate true a false b`.  A gate of two `base` operands is `base (x AND y)` (as `gateW`).
    Application binds tighter than the infix; nested gates are parenthesised.  Notation expands at elaboration.
    Rows: hex numbers, 16-bit fields, low field first: [family + 1, k, p_1 .. p_k, literal codes ...] where p_1 .. p_k are
    the parameters up to the last non-zero one (the decoder pads to 8 with zeros; negative parameters are stored +1000),
    and a literal code is `2 i + (1 if negated)` for variable number `i` (1-based in the name chunks of 200).
    The existing quad relation rows (krelOK) are family 24 (23 is the tie rule).  Tie families keep the tag parameters of T0/FORMAT.md, with the CNF variable numbers zeroed (family 20, 21, 26: all; 16:
    all; 23: the tfail variable `fv` (p7); 38: `y` (p1); 39: `v` (p1)).  Added: for family 32 kind 1 and family 35 kind 2
    the parameter p8 is `2 * view + (1 if k < 0 else 0)` of the `LS t s view k` line of the pair (t, s) (`lsTab` below). -/

